cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  RAISR-SME: a rapid AI-security readiness instrument for small and
  medium enterprises
message: >-
  This repository accompanies a manuscript that is currently under peer
  review. Author and affiliation metadata is withheld for anonymous
  review and will be added on acceptance. Until then, please cite the
  repository itself rather than attributing it to any individual.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Anonymous (author details withheld for peer review)
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the RAISR-SME instrument (item bank v1) and
  the analysis code behind its evaluation. The instrument is a 25-item,
  six-dimension self-assessment that returns a 0-100 exposure score, an
  ordinal band, and a ranked list of remediations, designed for
  completion by a single respondent in about twenty minutes. The
  repository contains three independent scoring engines verified against
  one another, a test suite covering polarity, monotonicity, band
  boundaries and cross-engine parity, and the scripts producing the
  cross-sectional (UK Cyber Security Breaches Survey, 2023-2025) and
  panel (UK Cyber Security Longitudinal Survey, waves 1-4) analyses. No
  survey microdata is redistributed; every source is documented with its
  public access route and a checksum.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - small and medium enterprises
  - risk assessment
  - self-assessment instrument
  - artificial intelligence adoption
  - survey methodology
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-20"
